delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attribute-groups/REPLACE_WITH_GROUP_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against a fresh disposable scratch group
  ("WC Test Group For Delete", id `6aa981b9a30ca5945169a248`, created and
  destroyed in this same run) on "David's Dev Account". Retested from
  scratch, since the original version of this file (named "Delete Product
  Attribute Group (Undeclared)") pointed at a throwaway id from an
  earlier session with no `example{}` block.

  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s 2026-09-15 refresh formally declares `DELETE`
  for `/product-attribute-groups/{identifier}` (previously undeclared but
  working, quirk #20). **Unlike most other resources touched in this
  refresh, `PATCH` is NOT newly declared for this resource** -- the spec
  still declares no `PATCH` here, so this file only covers `DELETE`
  (no combined PATCH+DELETE file was created for this resource).

  ## What it does
  `DELETE /product-attribute-groups/{id}` -- `204 No Content`, then `404`
  on a follow-up `GET` -- genuinely deleted, same pattern as every other
  resource confirmed in this project.
}

